    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1601">

                <pb facs="1011" n="895" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg895"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.62/107.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Special Agent
                        Carothers.</hi><anchor n="154" xml:id="d1601-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-11-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 7, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department informed that German Vice Consul at Guanajuato is proprietor of
                    Hacienda Santiago in Villanueva, Zacatecas, and that this property has been
                    seized by R. S. Garay, Jefe de Armas, who claims to be acting under orders from
                    General Villa.</p>
                <p>At request of German Embassy this capital, please bring to attention of General
                    Villa and use your best efforts to have this property restored to rightful
                    owner.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1601-f1" n="154" type="source" xml:id="d1601-f1-content">
                <p>Communicated to the German Embassy November 9, 1914.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
